tests/full/login -- the login gate (legion, Solaris level)
==========================================================

    GUEST_DISK=<image> make login-verify
    GUEST_DISK=<image> tests/full/login/run [FWDIR]
                                about a minute
    tests/full/login/run selftest
                                prove the detector on an empty disk (no image
                                needed)

What it does: boots legion's firmware set under QEMU, types `boot disk` at the
OpenBoot prompt and requires Solaris's `console login:`. The boot gate
(tests/full/boot) stops at the prompt and nothing else runs the guest kernel;
this is the gate that does. The set is built from this tree
(`make all TARGET=legion`), or taken as it is from FWDIR (for instance the
`legion` directory of an unpacked release: then it checks the released bytes).
-m follows the set (`.md-signature`, else the `memory` line of RELEASE-INFO
beside it, else 2048). It also checks that QEMU loaded all six firmware files
from that set.

The guest disk is not part of this repository: GUEST_DISK is a Solaris 10 disk
image with the hsimd driver for Legion's simulated disk. The OpenSPARC T1
archive has one, S10image/disk.s10hw2; about its hsimd driver see
Sun's OpenSPARC T2 legion/src/support/hsimd (a standalone copy:
https://github.com/artyom-tarasenko/hsimd)
Without it the gate is skipped (exit 3), and `make test-full` includes it only
when GUEST_DISK is set. QEMU is the distribution package, as for the other
gates (tests/lib/qemu.sh); the disk is attached read-only (the niagara machine
maps it as RAM, writes never reach the file).

Classification of the console, by the earliest marker:
  `console login:`           pass
  `panic[cpuN]`              fail, the panic line is printed
  `Last Trap: Level 14`      OpenBoot's loader flake (disk path: 0 of 100
                             boots on each of three QEMUs); retried (ATTEMPTS,
                             default 3), reported with a warning if a later
                             attempt passes
  any other OpenBoot trap    fail
  the OpenBoot prompt back
  after `boot disk`          fail ("did not boot")
  no new console output for T_STALL seconds (240), or no login within
  T_LOGIN (300)              fail

Exit: 0 login; 1 the guest did not get there; 2 could not run, no ok prompt,
or the Level 14 flake on every attempt; 3 skipped.
Env: GUEST_DISK, QEMU, OUTDIR (the console log is OUTDIR/legion.console),
ATTEMPTS, T_OK (120), T_LOGIN (300), T_STALL (240), BOOT_CMD.

Not covered: the pci configuration (it needs our patched QEMU), more than login
(no commands are run in the guest), RAM sizes above what stock QEMU boots with
this disk (legion's default 2048 is the limit, RELEASE-INFO).
